Jeremy Turner <turnerjer0000@i_like_to_pet_friendly_goats.com> writes:
> in my last big game, i had my main stash at about level 10.  i decided i 
> wanted to move it a lot deeper, but i (of course) couldn't lift the 
> chest, so i started digging holes underneath it.  dropped it down quite 
> a few levels, until it landed right next to a pool, on a level that was 
> full of them.  (i had forgotten about this level)
> 
> question is: could it have landed in a pool?  does anything prevent 
> this?

The game would have done its best to prevent its landing in a pool;
it'll try 4000 times to find a location that is dry movable-onto space
without a boulder on it.

> on a similar note... when falling through holes, does anything prevent 
> landing, say, in the middle of medusa's sea and death by drowning?

The constraints on this are, as far as I can see, even stricter; it'll
always try to place you in an open room space or a maze corridor, even
if you're in a form that could actually survive landing in water.

(You'd never land in the _middle_ of the sea, anyway, since Medusa's
level has defined arrival regions, and the one for arrival from above
is always to the left of the level.)

